From: Omarchy Mobile <omamobile@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: pmi8994_fg: keep a confirmed full reading steady

At termination the PMI8950 charger on a Redmi 4 Prime reports FULL and
charging in turn every few seconds. The counter-based capacity capped
every reading outside FULL at 99 %, so a full battery flickered between
99 and 100 %.

The cap exists for a full point estimated from the monotonic SOC, which
can sit too low, so charging past it doesn't read 100 % early. Apply it
only until a FULL report has set the full point.

---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/pmi8994_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/pmi8994_fg.c
@@ -112,6 +112,7 @@
 
 	/* Counter value taken as 100 %, and the last reading */
 	bool cc_anchored;
+	bool cc_full_seen;
 	s64 cc_full_uah;
 	s64 cc_last_uah;
 	ktime_t cc_last_time;
@@ -607,10 +608,11 @@
  * counter under load. Report the charge used since the battery was last
  * full instead. The counter value at a full charge (the charger reports
  * FULL) is 100 %; until the first one after boot, the 100 % point is
- * estimated from the monotonic SOC. A counter step larger than a battery
- * current can explain moves that point with it, so the reported capacity
- * stays continuous. Near empty, where the voltage is the better guide,
- * the lower of the two is reported.
+ * estimated from the monotonic SOC and the reading stays below 100 %.
+ * A counter step larger than a battery current can explain moves that
+ * point with it, so the reported capacity stays continuous. Near empty,
+ * where the voltage is the better guide, the lower of the two is
+ * reported.
  *
  * @param chip Pointer to chip
  * @param val Pointer to store value at
@@ -649,11 +651,19 @@
 	chip->cc_last_uah = cc;
 	chip->cc_last_time = now;
 
+	if (chip->status == POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL)
+		chip->cc_full_seen = true;
 	if (chip->status == POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL || cc > chip->cc_full_uah)
 		chip->cc_full_uah = cc;
 
 	cap = 100 - div_s64((chip->cc_full_uah - cc) * 100 + nom_uah / 2, nom_uah);
-	if (chip->status != POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL)
+	/*
+	 * An estimated full point can be too low, and charging past it must
+	 * not read 100 % before the charger terminates. Once a FULL report has
+	 * set it, the charger's own flapping between FULL and charging at
+	 * termination must not make the reading flicker.
+	 */
+	if (!chip->cc_full_seen && chip->status != POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL)
 		cap = min_t(s64, cap, 99);
 	if (soc <= CC_LOW_SOC)
 		cap = min_t(s64, cap, soc);
